 39	% 2026 revival styling (draft-mode rendering only, not historical): the
 40	% original \note was a bare \textwidth framebox dropped mid-paragraph — it
 41	% overflowed the right page edge, could not break across pages, and was
 42	% typographically indistinguishable from normative spec content. Re-set the
 43	% authors' editorial annotations so they read as manuscript notes: small
 44	% sans-serif on a tinted ground with a heavy colored left bar and a
 45	% small-caps "Draft note" label; mdframed lets long notes break over pages.
 46	\usepackage{mdframed}
 47	\definecolor{draftnotebar}{rgb}{0.72,0.29,0.11}
